"example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/waste#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:e03192eb8ac2cf8902","definition":"Material derived by mechanical and chemical erosion from the land, carried by streams to the sea.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/waste#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:3ce6cc04eca8bf85a3","definition":"Useless and contemptible.","example":"Niggas moves so waste / Please, come outside the house and show yourself / So I can say it to your face","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"derogatory, slang","register":"derogatory, slang","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/waste#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:62749172119cb5c28f","definition":"Uncultivated, uninhabited.","example":"SOo whanne syr Galahad was departed from the castel of maydens / he rode tyl he came to a waste forest / & there he mette with syre launcelot and syr Percyuale but they knewe hym not / for he was newe desguysed / Ryghte so syr launcelot his fader dressid his spere and brake it vpon syr Galahad","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"archaic","register":"archaic","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/waste#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:9655184b638f2de445","definition":"Barren; desert; empty.","example":"‘The stars,’ she whispers, ‘blindly run;\n⁠A web is wov’n across the sky;\n⁠From out waste places comes a cry,\nAnd murmurs from the dying sun: […]","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/waste#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:0ded1a406c84b9576c","definition":"Rejected as being defective; eliminated as being worthless; produced in excess.","example":"Oxygen levels on Earth skyrocketed 2.4 billion years ago, when cyanobacteria evolved photosynthesis: the ability to convert water and carbon dioxide into carbohydrates and waste oxygen using solar energy.","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/waste#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:869a4282e89acfda86","definition":"Superfluous; needless.","example":"","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/waste#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d43596f14528b6c79f","definition":"Dismal; gloomy; cheerless.","example":"the savage Baron's heart[…] became appalled as he gazed forward into the waste darkness of futurity.","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/waste#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:06f25842514727c0a0","definition":"Unfortunate; disappointing.","example":"","